---
import MainGridLayout from "@layouts/MainGridLayout.astro";
import { url } from "@utils/url-utils";
---

<MainGridLayout
	title="Content Rights and Licensing"
	description="Licensing scopes for Shots of Rhapsody software, articles, and media."
>
	<article class="rights-page custom-md prose dark:prose-invert">
		<h1>Content Rights and Licensing</h1>
		<p>Shots of Rhapsody contains software, original writing, original media, project branding, and third-party material. Those categories do not share one license.</p>

		<h2>Software and theme code — MIT</h2>
		<p>The root MIT License applies to repository software, configuration, and the Fuwari-derived theme code. It does not extend to article text, hero images, project artwork, branding, trademarks, or other creative media merely because those files are stored in the same repository.</p>

		<h2>Eleven Tai Song articles and hero images — All Rights Reserved</h2>
		<p>The eleven manifest-controlled articles and their author-controlled original hero images are marked per post as <strong>All Rights Reserved</strong>. Copyright remains with Tai Song. No permission to copy, redistribute, adapt, train on, or commercially reuse that writing or media is granted by this site.</p>
		<p>Tai Song's author master is the authority for each work. A historical Vocal link records earlier publication history only; it does not change the authority or license of the work published here.</p>

		<h2>Repository-only drafts</h2>
		<p>The four non-manifest posts are intentionally unpublished drafts. Posts without an explicit per-post license retain the site's existing <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a> fallback until separately reviewed. This policy does not silently relicense the eleven manifest-controlled works or revoke rights already granted under a valid earlier license.</p>

		<h2>Project media and branding</h2>
		<p>Project-specific artwork, favicons, names, and branding are not licensed by the root MIT License unless a file-specific notice expressly says otherwise. The unpublished legacy podcast bundle is retained outside the production content tree for history only; no publication or reuse permission is implied.</p>

		<h2>Third-party material</h2>
		<p>Third-party names, trademarks, fonts, packages, theme lineage, and externally sourced assets remain subject to their respective owners' terms. See the repository's <a href="https://github.com/Shots-of-Rhapsody/Shots-of-Rhapsody/blob/main/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">third-party notices</a>. Their presence here does not grant additional rights.</p>

		<p><a href={url("/")}>Return to Shots of Rhapsody</a></p>
	</article>
</MainGridLayout>

<style>
	.rights-page {
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		background: var(--paper-raised);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow);
		padding: clamp(1.4rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
	}
</style>
